      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're saying that the traditional model is basically the gold standard for development? It feels like you're saying anything else is essentially a step down or less effective for a kid. Is there any actual evidence that other structures are actually detrimental, or is it just that they aren't \"ideal\"?",
